{"step_index":39,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T10:46:34Z","content":"الـ subagent شغال بيبني الملفات. في نفس الوقت خليني أجهز الملف الرئيسي وملفات المطابقة:","tool_calls":[{"name":"invoke_subagent","args":{"Subagents":[{"Model":"inherit","Prompt":"Create the following files for the pharmacy drug matching project at d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy:\n\n## 1. src/match/__init__.py (empty)\n\n## 2. src/match/text_match.py\nText preprocessing and fuzzy matching module:\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Text cleaning and fuzzy matching for Arabic drug names.\"\"\"\n```\n\nFunctions:\n- normalize_text(text: str) -> str:\n  - Convert Arabic-Indic digits (٠-٩) to Western digits (0-9)\n  - Remove tatweel/kashida (ـ)\n  - Remove tashkeel/diacritics\n  - Normalize whitespace (multiple spaces to single)\n  - Strip leading/trailing whitespace\n  - Normalize different forms of alef (أ, إ, آ -> ا)\n  - Normalize taa marbuta (ة -> ه) for search purposes\n  - DO NOT remove any words, abbreviations, or numbers\n  - Return normalized text\n\n- find_candidates(query: str, items: list[str], threshold: float = 0.60, max_results: int = 5) -> list[tuple[str, float]]:\n  - Normalize both query and items\n  - Use rapidfuzz.fuzz.token_sort_ratio for scoring\n  - Also try rapidfuzz.fuzz.partial_ratio and take the max\n  - Return top matches above threshold as list of (original_item, score)\n  - Score is 0-100 from rapidfuzz, we normalize to 0-1\n\n- quick_match(query: str, item: str) -> float:\n  - Quick similarity score between two drug names\n  - Returns 0.0 to 1.0\n\n## 3. src/match/gemini_match.py\nGemini-based intelligent drug matching:\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Use Gemini to resolve ambiguous drug name matches.\"\"\"\n```\n\nFunctions:\n- match_with_gemini(shortage_name: str, candidates: list[dict], api_key: str, model: str = 'gemini-2.5-flash') -> dict:\n  - Takes a shortage drug name and list of candidate items from a warehouse\n  - Each candidate has: item_name_raw, source (filename)\n  - Sends to Gemini with a carefully crafted prompt\n  - The prompt asks Gemini to:\n    1. Compare the shortage drug name with each candidate\n    2. Consider: drug name, concentration/strength, dosage form, pack size\n    3. Return a JSON with: matched_index (or -1 if no match), confidence (high/medium/low), reason\n    4. If there's a clear match (same drug, same strength, same form) -> match\n    5. If drug name matches but strength/form differs -> no match\n    6. If ambiguous -> return confidence=low\n  - Uses google.genai client (the new SDK)\n  - Uses structured output (response_mime_type='application/json')\n  - Returns: {\"matched\": bool, \"matched_item\": str|None, \"confidence\": str, \"reason\": str}\n\n- batch_match_with_gemini(shortage_items: list[str], warehouse_items: list[str], api_key: str, model: str = 'gemini-2.5-flash') -> list[dict]:\n  - For efficiency, batch multiple shortage items in one Gemini call\n  - Send up to 10 shortage items at a time with the full warehouse list\n  - Ask Gemini to match each shortage item to the best warehouse item\n  - Returns list of match results\n\nThe Gemini prompt should be in Arabic and very specific:\n- Focus on: اسم الصنف, التركيز, الشكل الدوائي, حجم العبوة\n- Spelling differences are OK (the same drug with typos)\n- Different concentrations = different product (NOT a match)\n- Different forms (tablets vs syrup) = different product (NOT a match)\n- Missing info (no concentration listed) = ambiguous, not an automatic match\n\nUse the google.genai SDK:\n```python\nfrom google import genai\nclient = genai.Client(api_key=api_key)\nresponse = client.models.generate_content(\n    model=model,\n    contents=prompt,\n    config={'response_mime_type': 'application/json'}\n)\n```\n\n## 4. src/match/coordinator.py\nThe main coordinator that orchestrates matching across all warehouses:\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Coordinator: matches shortages against all warehouses.\"\"\"\n```\n\nClass Coordinator:\n- __init__(self, config: Config)\n- process(self, shortage_items: list[dict], warehouse_data: dict[str, list[dict]]) -> dict:\n  - warehouse_data maps warehouse_name -> list of items\n  - For each warehouse (can think of each as a sub-agent):\n    1. First pass: exact text matching (after normalization)\n    2. Second pass: fuzzy matching with RapidFuzz for unmatched items\n    3. Third pass: Gemini matching for remaining ambiguous cases\n  - Track results per warehouse:\n    - matched: list of (shortage_item, warehouse_item) confirmed matches\n    - needs_review: ambiguous matches\n  - After all warehouses processed:\n    - Compile which shortages found in which warehouses\n    - Identify shortages not found in any warehouse\n  - Returns: {\n      'warehouse_results': {name: {matched: [...], needs_review: [...]}},\n      'not_found': [...],  # items not in any warehouse\n      'summary': {total_shortages, matched_count, not_found_count, review_count}\n    }\n\n- _match_warehouse(self, shortage_items, warehouse_items, warehouse_name) -> dict:\n  - Process one warehouse (one sub-agent)\n  - Print progress in Arabic\n\n## 5. src/output/__init__.py (empty)\n\n## 6. src/output/excel_writer.py\nWrite the final Excel output:\n\nFunction write_results_excel(results: dict, output_path: Path):\n- Create workbook with openpyxl\n- Sheet 'ملخص' (summary): total shortages, matched %, per-warehouse counts\n- For each warehouse: sheet named after warehouse file (truncated to 31 chars for Excel limit)\n  - Columns: اسم الصنف المطلوب, اسم الصنف في المخزن, درجة التطابق\n  - Only confirmed matches\n- Sheet 'لم يُعثر عليه': shortages not found in any warehouse\n  - Columns: اسم الصنف, الملف المصدر\n- Sheet 'يحتاج مراجعة': ambiguous matches needing human review\n  - Columns: اسم الصنف المطلوب, اسم المرشح في المخزن, المخزن, السبب\n- Format: RTL, Arabic font, freeze top row, auto-filter\n- Header styling: dark teal background, white bold text\n\n## 7. main.py (at project root d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\main.py)\nMain entry point for CLI usage:\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Pharmacy Drug Matching Pipeline\n\nUsage:\n  python main.py --shortages <file> --warehouses <file1> <file2> ... --output <output.xlsx>\n\"\"\"\n```\n\n- Parse command line arguments with argparse\n- Load config from .env\n- Read shortage files\n- Read warehouse files (each file = one warehouse)\n- Run coordinator\n- Write Excel output\n- Print summary in Arabic\n\nMake all code clean with type hints, docstrings, and proper error handling.","Role":"Match and output builder","TypeName":"pharmacy-builder"}],"toolAction":"Building matching modules","toolSummary":"Match and output code"}}]}
